  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "Triple match – three 1v1s at once",
  "description": "Three separate 1v1 games are played at the same time on a small pitch with two goals, about 15 × 10 metres (not to scale – the pitch is drawn larger so the players are easy to see). Each pair has its own ball. Whoever has the ball attacks, and the roles switch the moment the ball is won. With all three duels sharing the same space it gets crowded and chaotic, so players keep meeting new 1v1 situations.\n\nAdjust the size: a smaller pitch means less time and more duels, a bigger one gives more time but easily turns into plain dribbling. With more players, set up two pitches side by side.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Attack: fake one way and go the other – finish the move with a change of pace."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Attack: keep your body between the defender and the ball."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Defence: stay goal-side, facing the attacker, and steer them towards the sideline."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Ask the players: what do you need to think about attacking 1v1 – and defending?"
    }
  ],
